A method's formals are declared on TypeElement; gendrake.ElementOf reads them itself (GitHub #11)

OWNING ISSUE: GitHub #11 (open; stays open). Nothing on the tracker was touched.

WHY. After 180a7ab `gendrake.ElementOf` still took one dependency of its own, `formals (TypeElement -> [TypeParameter])`:
`typeParameters` was declared on Dynamic alone, a definition holding a TypeElement could not reach it, and the emitter
supplied it through `elementFormals`, a match on the host class. TypeElement already declares six defaulted shared
fields, two of them (`parameters`, `body`) used by some kinds only. Recommended after 180a7ab; Dev answered "Journal
first" (chapters 134–136, 73f77c8) and then "Accepted, build it".

WHAT.
- draco.TypeElement: `fix typeParameters [TypeParameter] []`, the seventh defaulted shared field.
- draco.Dynamic: its own `elements` declaration of `typeParameters` removed; the factory parameter and its binding stay,
  so Dynamic alone supplies the field.
- gendrake.ElementOf: factory `element`, `level`; `loc given [TypeParameter] element.typeParameters`; the recursion is
  `ElementOf(member, depth)`.
- Three surfaces authored in drake, their JSON `DrakeCLI parse`, their Scala the generator's output: the family file
  TypeElement.scala (generate-multi over the fourteen family definitions) changes in four places — the trait's defaulted
  line, the encoder writing the field in the shared list when non-empty where it had a Dynamic branch, Dynamic's trait
  losing its abstract member — and ElementOf.scala loses the parameter. The shape of the regenerated family file was
  NOT probed before the recommendation and came out as expected.
- Drake.scala: `elementFormals` removed, `elementLines` calling `ElementOf(element, level)`; `refuseElement` still
  validates a method's formals before anything renders.
- Tests: ElementOfTest's formals case reads them from a Dynamic element and asserts the empty default on another kind;
  FormalOfTest reads `_.typeParameters`. No test added, no corpus type added.

THE CARRIER DOES NOT MOVE: an empty list is elided and only Dynamic's factory supplies the field, so no definition's
JSON or drake surface changes beyond the three trios.

WHAT STAYS a dependency: `elementText`, passed by the emitter to the section transforms, because the element refusals
are still the emitter's. NOT BUILT, none accepted: the refusals ahead of rendering; a failure form for the guards.

VERIFIED before the gate: `DrakeCLI check` reads surface drift 0, json drift 0 over main and mods; the three trios are
stable on regeneration with the recompiled engine. Direct run of every discovered suite on freshly compiled classes
with current main, mods and test resources on the loader roots: 1269 tests / 92 suites including discovery, zero
failed, canceled, ignored, pending or aborted, green on its FIRST run. Headlines that move, by the two elements net
removed (ElementOf's parameter and binding, Dynamic's declaration; TypeElement's added): Element 1117 elements (1364
lines), Slot 1099 value-type slots (81 arrows parenthesized), TypeForm 2161 forms (483 trees, 1678 leaves), type leaves
1678, host text 21 leaves of 2807 in the 11 named seams. Unchanged: parse scope 128 + 73 with 0 held back, surface
losses 0 across 201 types, DomainAspect and DracoAspect 128, GenDrake 126 of 126, rule 24, actor 15, 94 records, 4 codec
sections, Definition 201 surfaces from 539 sections, Expression 661 values (483 trees, 178 leaves), Formal 36 formals
(33 lists, 7 bounded), example gate 48 / 0, scenario 23 clean, the PON pair 42 and 7 as suspended, the rete finding
categorical. The tree afterwards held the intended changes only.

DEV'S GATE (2026-11-14, full `sbt test`, output pasted): Tests: succeeded 1269, failed 0, canceled 0, ignored 0, pending
0; every headline matching the direct run, the five moved ones included; green on its first run. The baseline stays
